WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.649
The paper makes three contributions.

00:00:03.729 --> 00:00:07.378
First,

00:00:07.458 --> 00:00:11.107
a rigorous case study establishing that improving
graph neural network expressivity does

00:00:11.187 --> 00:00:14.836
not mitigate poor calibration under distribution shift.

00:00:14.916 --> 00:00:18.565
Second, G-Delta-UQ,

00:00:18.645 --> 00:00:22.295
a novel single-model uncertainty method that
extends the stochastic centering framework to structured graph data and,

00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:26.024
crucially,

00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:29.753
supports partial stochasticity so that only part of
the network is made stochastic.

00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:33.482
Third, an extensive empirical evaluation spanning
covariate, concept,

00:00:33.562 --> 00:00:37.211
and graph size shifts, across the safety-critical
tasks of calibration,

00:00:37.291 --> 00:00:40.940
generalization gap prediction, and
out-of-distribution detection.
